  "rule": "A solid colour-5 key rectangle contains isolated coloured dots and is a scaled map of the same-coloured shapes elsewhere. Normalise dot positions inside the key and shape bbox centres inside the all-shapes bbox. Pair each dot with a shape by minimum total squared distance. Recolour each shape with its dot's colour and leave the key unchanged.",
  "scope": "Supported: 2..5 shapes on a compressed 2x2/2x3/3x2/3x3 slot lattice, with jittered placement, variable cell sizes and random 8-connected (often mirror-symmetric, sometimes diagonal-only) sprites. The key is 5..10 per side and placed left/right/above/below the shape field, with random gap and margins. Dot colours and the shape colour are random. Background 0 and key colour 5 are fixed, as in all fixtures. Not supported: more than 5 shapes, irregular non-lattice layouts, and multiple keys. Border dots are now supported; random mode honors width, height and shape_color.",
  "constraints": [
    "Exactly one dot per shape; dot colours are distinct and differ from the shape colour, 0 and 5",
    "Dots may lie inside or on the key border, with pairwise Chebyshev distance >= 2; colour-5 cells remain connected.",
    "Shapes are separated from each other and from the key by at least one blank row/column, including diagonally",
    "Each shape bbox is fully spanned by its cells, and the shape is 8-connected",
    "The key's colour-5 cell count exceeds every shape's size, so the key is the largest object",
    "Background 0 is strictly the most frequent colour",
    "The intended pairing beats every other permutation by at least 0.1 in total normalised squared distance, so the matching is unambiguous",
    "Grid sides are at most 30"
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Shapes always come from a lattice of slots mirrored by the dot lattice; free-form layouts are not sampled",
    "The ambiguity check uses the stated normalised min-cost matching criterion. Scenes where a human might read the map differently, but the margin is large, are not specially filtered",
    "Raises RuntimeError if 2000 sampling attempts fail, which is expected to be practically unreachable"
  ],
